# Allocation Rules

Use adaptive distributions.
Consider total points, songs, score density, fit weighting, and points-to-songs ratio.
Do not force symmetry.
Ask for compressed, balanced, or top-heavy if unclear.

## Tiering

Allocate by tiers, not by raw blended decimals. Group near-ties into one tier and give them
equal points; never split a near-tie. Equal music with a small fit gap (≈≤3) stays in the same
tier. Keep the spread modest (top tier ≤ ~2-3× a lower tier) but avoid flat equality.

## Fit-weighted rounds

1. Qualifier gate first: below the fit cutoff (usually "good fit" = solid+) earns no points,
   regardless of music. A loved-but-poor-fit song only takes a leftover point.
2. combined = wFit×fit + wMusic×music (record weights; fit-heavy by default).
3. Tier qualifiers by fit band, then music within a band; small fit gaps do not override equal
   music scores.
4. A song carried only by fit (music lagging its tier) may be bumped down one tier — document
   the call.
